  <p>
    Santa Clara rewrote its fence and wall chapter in 2022, and it is one of the more process-driven cities around St. George:
    every fence and wall system gets a review by the building official before it goes in, and the city offers a fence permit
    application for the purpose. This page summarizes Santa Clara City Code chapter 17.28 as read on September 26, 2026.
  </p>

  <h2>Santa Clara fence and wall rules at a glance</h2>
  <IconList items={rules} />

  <h2>Heights on a typical lot</h2>
  <p>
    On an interior lot, a 6-foot fence may run along the side and rear property lines, starting 15 feet back from the front
    property line where the line is measured from the back of the sidewalk, or 25 feet back where it is measured from the back of
    the curb. In the front setback, fences, walls, and retaining walls stay at 3 feet, unless the fence is at least 50 percent open,
    in which case it may be 4 feet tall if set 1 foot behind the property line.
  </p>
  <p>
    A fence and wall system built entirely on one lot can reach 9 feet in total, and where a fence sits on a retaining wall on a
    shared property line, the combination is limited to 9 feet measured from the lower side (§17.28.030). Grade may not be bermed
    up to gain height.
  </p>

  <h2>Retaining walls</h2>
  <p>
    Santa Clara caps retaining walls at 6 feet. Above 4 feet, the wall must be engineered and approved under International
    Residential Code standards, and a building permit is required once the wall exceeds 4 feet measured from the bottom of the
    footing, a different measuring point from St. George's. Systems taller than 6 feet must be terraced into benches at a 1:1
    offset, and retaining walls must be moisture-proofed on the retained side below grade. A rock wall no more than 4 feet tall
    with a slope no steeper than 1:1 is not treated as a retaining wall under §17.28.060.
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    No Santa Clara fence or wall company publishes prices. As of {COST_AS_OF}, typical residential fence projects in the St. George
    area run about {fenceProject.low}–{fenceProject.high} installed, and CMU block walls about {blockWall.perSqFt} per square foot. Where
    Santa Clara requires an engineered design, add that fee; the <a href="/retaining-wall-cost-st-george-ut/">retaining wall cost
    guide</a> shows typical engineering costs.
  </p>

